# engine-core Module Rules

Reference: `docs/tech-spec.md` §4.2, §5, §6. Architecture overview: `README.md`.

- **Role:** Orchestrates engine lifecycle, config, backend selection, and the producer thread. Loads tracks via `AudioSource` and feeds decoded samples into `engine-dsp` decks.
- **Module layout:** Keep responsibilities split across files; do not collapse back into a single `lib.rs`.
  - `lib.rs` — module declarations and public re-exports only
  - `config.rs` — `EngineConfig`, `DeviceConfig`, `AdvancedConfig`, `AudioConfig` (TOML load/save)
  - `engine.rs` — `Engine` public API (`new`, `start`/`stop`, `load_track`, `play`/`pause`, bus/device helpers)
  - `backend.rs` — `create_backend`, `AudioBackend` factory, `AudioBackendTrait` re-export
  - `producer.rs` — ring buffer setup, `MasterStreamSetup`, producer thread loop
  - `callback.rs` — `ConsumerCallback` (ring-buffer consumer for the audio device callback)
  - `audio_source/` — `FileAudioSource`; re-exports `AudioSource` / `LoadedAudio` from `audio-core`
- **Engine API:** `Engine::new(config)`, `start`/`stop`, `load_track(deck_id, &impl AudioSource)`, `play`/`pause(deck_id)`, `set_bus_device(bus, device, channels)`. Do **not** take a bare path in `load_track`; callers pass an `AudioSource` (e.g. `FileAudioSource::new(path)`).
- **Audio loading:** Trait and `LoadedAudio` live in `audio-core`. Disk loading is `FileAudioSource` in this crate (uses `codec`). New origins implement `AudioSource` without changing `Engine`.
- **Config:** TOML via `EngineConfig::from_toml_file` / `to_toml_file`. Fields include `sample_rate`, `buffer_size`, `low_latency`, `backend`, buses/devices, optional advanced/audio sections.
- **Threading:** Producer thread (engine-controlled) runs DSP and writes interleaved stereo to a lock-free ring buffer. Consumer is the backend audio callback (`ConsumerCallback`). No allocations in the callback path.
- **Ring buffer:** Preallocate; buffer at least N × frames_per_buffer (current multiplier is higher than the minimum N ≥ 8) to tolerate producer jitter.
- **Backend selection:** Runtime choice via config (`auto` / `cpal` / `miniaudio` / `null`). All backends compiled in; no dynamic loading. Use `AudioBackend::list_names()` / `AudioBackend::new(name)` for discovery before constructing an engine.
